      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CRUNCHYLOVER (1) was 1.4 metres away in third at Pinjarra over 2185m last start at her first run back from a spell. Has the benefit of a good draw. Leading hope in this comparable race. REINE DU SOLEIL (7) finished fifth last start, beaten 16 metres at Gloucester Park over 2130m. Talented and has plenty of upside. Has ability and should be right in the finish. ELQUESTRO (6) missed the placings two runs back then did a great job to finish 12 metres back in third despite breaking after interference in the run over 2050m at Collie two weeks ago. It doesn't get any easier but he is going well enough to be competitive. THE BELL HUEY (5) is worth some thought after his last-start fourth over 2130m at Gloucester Park on November 4.",
